WEBVTT

00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.754 --> 00:00:06.510
In this lesson, we do volume lashes with handmade fans, step by step.

00:00:06.999 --> 00:00:09.150
Throughout the set, remember three things:

00:00:09.498 --> 00:00:14.333
the client's eyes stay closed, each fan goes on exactly one natural lash,

00:00:14.283 --> 00:00:16.430
and glue never touches the skin.

00:00:17.104 --> 00:00:17.879
Step one:

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:18.999
preparation.

00:00:19.326 --> 00:00:22.359
This is exactly the same as in the classic practice lesson:

00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:27.680
consultation and allergy questions, a comfortable position, cleansing,

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.719
under eye pads, and brushing.

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:32.919
If you have not seen it yet, watch that lesson first.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.334
While you brush, look closely at the natural lashes in each zone,

00:00:37.284 --> 00:00:39.879
to choose how many lashes go in each fan:

00:00:40.121 --> 00:00:45.639
strong lashes take fans with more lashes, weak lashes take fewer, lighter ones.

00:00:46.237 --> 00:00:46.932
Step two:

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.212
set up your station.

00:00:48.678 --> 00:00:52.612
A volume lash tray, very fine lashes, arranged by length.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.252
A jade stone with a fresh drop of glue.

00:00:55.661 --> 00:00:56.532
And your tweezers:

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.384
a straight one for isolating, and volume tweezers, long and angled at the tip,

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.012
for making and placing fans.

00:01:03.355 --> 00:01:06.612
A lash wand and small cotton swabs, all disposable.

00:01:07.027 --> 00:01:09.652
The glue bottle, capped straight after you take the glue.

00:01:10.325 --> 00:01:11.182
Step three:

00:01:11.588 --> 00:01:12.782
pick up the lashes.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:17.536
Hold the volume tweezers, and lay the tips across a few lashes on the strip,

00:01:17.486 --> 00:01:19.102
near the tips of the lashes.

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:21.982
Pick up as many lashes as you want in the fan.

00:01:22.383 --> 00:01:26.462
Grip very lightly, like holding a thread, and never squeeze.

00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:29.418
Take lashes from the edge of the strip inward,

00:01:29.368 --> 00:01:32.302
so the rest of the strip stays neat and undisturbed.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:35.262
When you are starting out, count the lashes to be sure.

00:01:35.509 --> 00:01:38.542
Over time, your eyes and hands will get used to it.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:39.921
Step four:

00:01:40.184 --> 00:01:41.041
open the fan.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:46.321
Keep that light grip, then slowly slide the tweezers toward the base of the lashes.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.401
As the tweezers slide down, the lashes spread out by themselves.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:54.801
Some technicians roll or tilt the tweezers instead, to open the fan.

00:01:55.228 --> 00:02:00.235
Either way is fine, as long as, at the end, you close the tweezers at the base,

00:02:00.185 --> 00:02:03.121
so the base of the fan is very small and neat.

00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:05.521
Then lift the fan gently off the strip.

00:02:05.845 --> 00:02:11.200
A narrow fan gives a sharper look, a wide fan gives a fuller, softer look.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.191
But never open it too wide,

00:02:13.141 --> 00:02:16.961
because a fan that is too wide will touch the next natural lash.

00:02:17.622 --> 00:02:18.566
Step five:

00:02:18.755 --> 00:02:20.566
check the fan before you take glue.

00:02:20.892 --> 00:02:22.726
Is the base small and closed?

00:02:23.074 --> 00:02:25.605
Do the lashes spread evenly and symmetrically?

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.286
Is the number of lashes right?

00:02:27.789 --> 00:02:32.020
If the fan is lopsided, the base is wide, or lashes are stuck together,

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:33.846
throw it away and make another.

00:02:34.348 --> 00:02:36.646
Remaking a fan takes only a few seconds.

00:02:36.915 --> 00:02:40.406
Putting a bad fan on the client's eye costs far more than that.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:41.923
Step six:

00:02:42.213 --> 00:02:43.043
take the glue.

00:02:43.506 --> 00:02:47.693
Touch only the base of the fan to the edge of the glue drop, very lightly,

00:02:47.643 --> 00:02:48.643
then pull it out.

00:02:49.152 --> 00:02:52.963
Never dip deep, and never let the glue creep up between the lashes.

00:02:53.312 --> 00:02:55.123
A thin coat, just enough.

00:02:55.622 --> 00:02:58.963
If the base has picked up a big blob of glue, do not hesitate:

00:02:59.154 --> 00:03:01.203
throw that fan away and make a new one.

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:05.467
A glue drop left on the stone too long thickens and bonds poorly,

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:08.323
so change it often, as the glue maker instructs.

00:03:08.884 --> 00:03:09.776
Step seven:

00:03:10.117 --> 00:03:10.976
isolation.

00:03:11.378 --> 00:03:14.464
Your non dominant hand holds the straight tweezers,

00:03:14.414 --> 00:03:18.096
and isolates a single natural lash, as in the classic lesson.

00:03:18.524 --> 00:03:19.616
Isolate cleanly.

00:03:19.951 --> 00:03:23.650
Because the fan is wide, if just one neighboring lash stays close,

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.696
the glue will catch it straight away.

00:03:26.296 --> 00:03:27.073
Step eight:

00:03:27.258 --> 00:03:28.353
attach the fan.

00:03:28.828 --> 00:03:32.064
Place the base of the fan on the isolated natural lash,

00:03:32.014 --> 00:03:34.033
so the base wraps around the lash,

00:03:34.142 --> 00:03:35.473
in the direction it grows.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:40.338
The base of the fan sits about 0.5 to 1 mm from the eyelid skin,

00:03:40.288 --> 00:03:41.953
never touching the skin.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:46.935
Press it gently along the lash, hold still for a moment so the glue grabs,

00:03:46.885 --> 00:03:48.433
then release the tweezers.

00:03:48.676 --> 00:03:52.193
The fan must sit evenly, not flipped, not twisted.

00:03:52.613 --> 00:03:56.509
If the fan sits crooked, take it off right away, before the glue sets,

00:03:56.459 --> 00:03:57.553
and make a new fan.

00:03:57.983 --> 00:04:00.113
Never try to fix it once the glue is dry.

00:04:00.775 --> 00:04:05.177
As with classic, never attach lashes that sit right next to each other,

00:04:05.127 --> 00:04:06.281
one after another.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:11.161
Attach one fan at the outer corner, then in the middle, then at the inner corner,

00:04:11.111 --> 00:04:11.881
then go back.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:15.757
That way, the glue of the previous fan has time to cure,

00:04:15.707 --> 00:04:17.881
and the fans do not stick together.

00:04:18.538 --> 00:04:19.410
Step nine:

00:04:19.585 --> 00:04:20.690
check for stickies.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.354
After each zone, glide the straight tweezers lightly through the lashes,

00:04:25.304 --> 00:04:26.370
from base to tip:

00:04:26.714 --> 00:04:30.210
each fan must stand on its own, on a single natural lash.

00:04:30.638 --> 00:04:34.450
If you see a sticky, separate it right away, very gently.

00:04:34.958 --> 00:04:37.010
Look at the lashes from several angles:

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.010
from above, and from the side.

00:04:39.361 --> 00:04:41.810
Some stickies only show when you look from the side.

00:04:42.414 --> 00:04:43.104
For length:

00:04:43.134 --> 00:04:47.104
shortest in the inner corner, then gradually longer toward the outer corner.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.418
At the inner corner, the natural lashes are short and weak,

00:04:51.368 --> 00:04:53.344
so use fans with fewer lashes,

00:04:53.373 --> 00:04:54.464
short and light.

00:04:54.871 --> 00:04:59.372
In the middle and at the outer corner, the natural lashes are usually stronger,

00:04:59.322 --> 00:05:01.344
and can take fans with more lashes,

00:05:01.541 --> 00:05:03.824
but always within what each lash can carry.

00:05:04.066 --> 00:05:08.144
Choosing a style for each eye shape, we will learn in the lash mapping lesson.

00:05:08.796 --> 00:05:09.681
Step ten:

00:05:09.857 --> 00:05:10.561
finishing.

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:14.641
Brush the lashes again, and compare both eyes so they match.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.190
Remove the pads very gently, while the client's eyes are still closed,

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.201
then let her open her eyes slowly.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:25.681
If her eyes sting or water, let her close them again and rest a moment.

00:05:26.094 --> 00:05:28.321
Aftercare is as in the classic lesson:

00:05:28.502 --> 00:05:32.002
keep the lashes dry for as long as the glue maker advises,

00:05:31.952 --> 00:05:34.321
no oil based products at the lash base,

00:05:34.403 --> 00:05:38.801
brush them every day, no rubbing, and book a refill after two to three weeks.

00:05:39.401 --> 00:05:40.809
Once the client has gone:

00:05:40.914 --> 00:05:44.649
used wands, swabs and pads go into a lidded bin.

00:05:45.157 --> 00:05:48.089
Tweezers are cleaned and disinfected after every client.

00:05:48.598 --> 00:05:51.209
Your first volume set will take a very long time.

00:05:51.373 --> 00:05:52.169
Do not worry.

00:05:52.431 --> 00:05:56.089
With every set, your hands will get more even, and faster.

00:05:56.357 --> 00:05:59.049
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
